jobs.description:
Would you like to get a glimpse into the world of logistics? Whether you’re ready for a new job as a Logistic Worker or just want to explore the industry, we’d love to welcome you to our Meet & Greet in Breda on September 30! At BPO Services, you’ll start right away with a 7-month contract! Interested? Sign up by simply applying for this job opening.

What we offer
- A monthly salary of € 2.596,03 on 35 hour basis;
- A place on a close-knit, international team
- An immediate 7-month contract
- A nice cafeteria with a cozy “chill corner”
- Attractive benefits under the collective agreement
- Travel allowance of €0.23 per km.

Who you are
As a Warehouse Employee, you don’t mind doing physical work. Together with your coworkers, you’ll ensure that the warehouse operates 24 hours a day. To keep the warehouse running 24 hours a day, you’ll work on a 3-shift schedule. If you only want to work on Saturday’s then there will be no 3-shift schedule. You can choose the morning (06:00-15:00) or evening shift (15:00-00:00).

- You speak Dutch or English;
- You are interested in a long term employmentship;
- You are available to work in Breda;
- You are willing to work in three shifts or only the Saturdays without 3 shifts;
- You are willing to perform physical labor;
- You have your own transportation.

What will you do
As a Logistic Worker, you’re the indispensable link in the sorting center. Together with your team, you ensure that thousands of secondhand treasures and packages find their way seamlessly to buyers in the Netherlands, Belgium, and France every day. It’s an active job where time flies by! You will be working in a 3-shift rotation with the following work hours: 7:00 AM to 3:00 PM, 3:00 PM to 11:00 PM, and 11:00 PM to 7:00 AM. Your daily tasks include:

- You unload incoming containers full of packages and immediately start the sorting process;
- You place the packages on the high-tech sorting belts and platforms so they’re routed to the correct destination at li

As a Production Employee, you help keep the production process running smoothly. Together with your colleagues, you make sure the products are produced, packed and checked correctly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Operating and monitoring production machines;
- Packing and repacking soft drink products;
- Checking the quality of products and packaging;
- Keeping the production line running smoothly;
- Identifying small problems or disruptions;
- Keeping your workplace clean and safe;
- Working in different areas of the production process;
- Helping and supporting new colleagues.

Working hours

You will work full-time in a 2-shift schedule:

- Morning shift: 07:00 - 15:00
- Afternoon shift: 15:00 - 23:00

Your hourly wage is €17.52 gross, including a 13% shift allowance.

- You are available full-time;
- You are willing to work in two shifts;
- You enjoy working in a production environment;
- You are interested in machines and technology;
- You work safely and accurately;
- You can communicate in Dutch and/or English;
- Experience in production or logistics is an advantage, but not always necessary;
- A VCA or forklift certificate is an advantage, or you are willing to obtain certificates.

Most importantly, you are motivated and ready to work!
